    "module_designation": "Multi-Dimensional Measuring Instrument",
    "description": "Automatic multi-dimensional measuring instrument (MDMI) designated MV-DLxxxx-0yy-y, where x and y may be 0-9 or A-Z and represent models with different housing colour, baseline or scan rate. Intended for scanning the dimensions of rectangular boxes moved on a transport belt below the camera. The instrument can measure objects of different colours and sizes but does not measure irregular objects. Consists of a 3D laser camera placed on a portal or mounted in the ceiling; the pictures from the camera of the object are transmitted to a PC, which analyses them and calculates the dimensions. The PC software includes a data storage device working as an alibi memory in which all performed measurements are stored; alternatively measurements are sent to a central system."
